WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:01.740
It's great to welcome to the program today.

00:00:01.740 --> 00:00:08.020
David Shimer, who's a fellow at Yale University
and also author of the book Rigged America,

00:00:08.020 --> 00:00:12.090
Russia and One Hundred Years of Covert Electoral
Interference.

00:00:12.090 --> 00:00:17.140
David, the title already tells us a lot about
Mike.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:23.250
My first question, but in the in the discussion
about alleged Russian interference in the

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:29.269
2016 election and planned interference in
2020, there's this bigger discussion of how

00:00:29.269 --> 00:00:33.220
long has trans national election interference
been going on?

00:00:33.220 --> 00:00:34.220
So.

00:00:34.220 --> 00:00:36.930
So maybe let's start there where we're how
long has it been going on?

00:00:36.930 --> 00:00:37.930
Sure.

00:00:37.930 --> 00:00:43.530
So what I do in my book is I restore history
to the subject of Koeberg electoral interference

00:00:43.530 --> 00:00:49.760
because a myth that is prevailing in our discourse
today is that Russian interference in the

00:00:49.760 --> 00:00:55.800
2016 election was somehow new or novel or
unprecedented.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:59.830
And that's dangerous because it something
street, it is unprecedented.

00:00:59.830 --> 00:01:02.970
Then it's treated as something that there's
no history behind.

00:01:02.970 --> 00:01:06.690
And it's very easy to manipulate how people
perceive it and whether people even believe

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.690
it happened.

00:01:07.690 --> 00:01:12.860
And what I do in this book is show that, in
fact, for the last century, beginning in 1919,

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:17.830
the Soviet Union, for a period the United
States and the now Putin's Russia have been

00:01:17.830 --> 00:01:19.970
interfering in elections all over the world.

00:01:19.970 --> 00:01:20.970
I show where.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:21.970
I show why.

00:01:21.970 --> 00:01:28.220
I show how they have used their intelligence
services to direct and disrupt open elections.

00:01:28.220 --> 00:01:33.450
And I then use that history to shine new light
on what actually happened in 2016, how we

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:38.530
can understand what Putin achieved and what
we should be doing now to defend our elections

00:01:38.530 --> 00:01:41.640
both before November and thereafter.

00:01:41.640 --> 00:01:46.300
So there's like five different branches that
we could explore.

00:01:46.300 --> 00:01:48.780
Let I'll just pick one to start with.

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:55.340
What would be since 1919 the most successful
examples of that interference?

00:01:55.340 --> 00:01:56.340
Sure.

00:01:56.340 --> 00:02:00.570
So there's one case that that it was actually
what sparked my interest in this whole subject,

00:02:00.570 --> 00:02:07.360
which was in 1972, there was a vote of no
confidence in the chancellor of West Germany,

00:02:07.360 --> 00:02:08.360
Willy Brandt.

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:12.000
And this and this vote of no confidence came
at a pivotal moment in the history of the

00:02:12.000 --> 00:02:13.000
Cold War.

00:02:13.000 --> 00:02:16.080
Willy Brandt had been executing a foreign
policy of Ostpolitik.

00:02:16.080 --> 00:02:20.050
He had been reestablishing relations with
the Soviet Union, with the Eastern Bloc.

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:26.170
A real pivotal Cold War figure, which, as
a result of his groundbreaking policies, sparked

00:02:26.170 --> 00:02:29.250
dissent within his parliamentary coalition.

00:02:29.250 --> 00:02:32.100
And there was a vote to remove him from office
as chancellor.

00:02:32.100 --> 00:02:37.670
That vote failed by two votes, just two after
which he was able to ratify the treaty he'd

00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:43.430
been pursuing and really pursue to completion
or as he saw his foreign policy.

00:02:43.430 --> 00:02:48.640
And what I reveal in the book is that there
was a covert operation executed by East German

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:52.820
intelligence ordered by Moscow to purchase
those two votes.

00:02:52.820 --> 00:02:57.380
And I interviewed one of the intelligence
officers who participated in that operation.

00:02:57.380 --> 00:02:59.540
He now lives just outside of Berlin.

00:02:59.540 --> 00:03:01.069
I spent about half a day with him.

00:03:01.069 --> 00:03:04.670
I went through a bunch of different archives
and re-created this story.

00:03:04.670 --> 00:03:08.950
And it's a story of targeting two vulnerable
lawmakers who were very corruptible because

00:03:08.950 --> 00:03:14.810
of their womanizing, their deaths, their alcoholism,
turning them, drawing them in slowly and then

00:03:14.810 --> 00:03:18.540
paying them each fifty thousand deutschmarks
in exchange for their extensions and then

00:03:18.540 --> 00:03:19.610
covering it up.

00:03:19.610 --> 00:03:25.180
And it took decades for this operation to
come out and had the East German intelligence

00:03:25.180 --> 00:03:27.950
agency not interfered in this vote.

00:03:27.950 --> 00:03:29.379
The outcome would have been different.

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:33.690
Brandt would have gone from power and the
trajectory of the Cold War would have changed.

00:03:33.690 --> 00:03:37.220
And it did not as a direct result of covert
interference.

00:03:37.220 --> 00:03:40.380
Just briefly, do you know offhand how much?

00:03:40.380 --> 00:03:44.580
Fifty thousand deutschmarks then is roughly
like how many dollars today would we be thinking

00:03:44.580 --> 00:03:45.580
about?

00:03:45.580 --> 00:03:47.790
Like a little less than one hundred thousand
dollars.

00:03:47.790 --> 00:03:48.790
OK.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.540
So it's not a crazy amount?

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:55.280
No, certainly given the the way in which it
redirected the trajectory of things at the

00:03:55.280 --> 00:03:56.280
time.

00:03:56.280 --> 00:04:03.180
Now, as the sort of disclaimer moment, you
we are not arguing here that Russia is the

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:04.650
only country that does this.

00:04:04.650 --> 00:04:08.760
We are just we happen to be talking about
Russia, but that's a common defense that no

00:04:08.760 --> 00:04:11.390
one other countries also do this.

00:04:11.390 --> 00:04:14.490
And number two, the U.S. also does this elsewhere.

00:04:14.490 --> 00:04:16.489
You're not denying either of those assertions?

00:04:16.489 --> 00:04:19.810
No, I'm denying I'm denying neither of those
assertions.

00:04:19.810 --> 00:04:24.439
But I do make the argument in my book that
the story of covert electoral interference

00:04:24.439 --> 00:04:26.340
is primarily to this point.

00:04:26.340 --> 00:04:31.779
This may change now moving forward, but to
this point has primarily been a story of Moscow

00:04:31.779 --> 00:04:33.099
and Washington.

00:04:33.099 --> 00:04:38.099
So between 1919, in 1947, the Soviet Union
was interfering in elections all over the

00:04:38.099 --> 00:04:44.389
world with brief interruptions and very intensely
between 45 and 47 across Eastern Europe between

00:04:44.389 --> 00:04:46.639
1948 and 1991.

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:50.969
The CIA and the KGB were going toe to toe
in elections all over the world in order to

00:04:50.969 --> 00:04:55.089
either seek to defeat or advance leftist candidates.

00:04:55.089 --> 00:05:00.180
And since 1991, Vladimir Putin's regime has
rediscovered and enhance the weapon of covert

00:05:00.180 --> 00:05:02.449
electoral interference using the Internet.

00:05:02.449 --> 00:05:06.770
He is once again targeting elections all over
the world in order to support authoritarian

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.339
minded and divisive candidates.

00:05:09.339 --> 00:05:13.990
And now one of the countries under attack
and a real meaningful way is America itself.

00:05:13.990 --> 00:05:15.599
So this is a very old story.

00:05:15.599 --> 00:05:19.490
And there are many lessons to draw from that
story as we seek to understand our present

00:05:19.490 --> 00:05:20.490
moment.

00:05:20.490 --> 00:05:23.629
It is not accurate to say that it is just
Russia that has been executing these sorts

00:05:23.629 --> 00:05:24.629
of operations.

00:05:24.629 --> 00:05:28.279
But we also shouldn't minimize the role of
Moscow in this history because Moscow really

00:05:28.279 --> 00:05:30.460
has been the pioneer.

00:05:30.460 --> 00:05:35.009
Beginning with Vladimir Lenin in 1919 to the
regime of Vladimir Putin today.

00:05:35.009 --> 00:05:37.189
So what was done?

00:05:37.189 --> 00:05:38.539
In 2016.

00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:42.780
And I think maybe what would be useful would
be to contextualize it in, you know, when

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:46.599
you have an election that ultimately comes
down to about seventy five thousand votes

00:05:46.599 --> 00:05:51.250
in three states and otherwise would have would
have been a Hillary Clinton win.

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:59.119
We have to balance what Russia did with James
Comey opting to do a second presser about

00:05:59.119 --> 00:06:03.539
Hillary Clinton's emails with targeted social
media campaigns.

00:06:03.539 --> 00:06:08.279
Hillary Clinton not going to win, Scott, right
like we can when it's so close.

00:06:08.279 --> 00:06:09.279
It's hard to say.

00:06:09.279 --> 00:06:13.430
One thing was the difference maker, but that
still means we should explore.

00:06:13.430 --> 00:06:15.520
What exactly did Russia do?

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:21.520
Exactly, and I think it's a real trap to falling
to the question of effectiveness when it comes

00:06:21.520 --> 00:06:25.559
to operations to manipulate people, because
there are two ways to manipulate in an election

00:06:25.559 --> 00:06:29.729
to alter actual ballots and to manipulate
minds, public opinion.

00:06:29.729 --> 00:06:31.550
And as I said, I've scoured this history.

00:06:31.550 --> 00:06:35.889
I interviewed more than 130 people, eight
former CIA directors, gone through archives

00:06:35.889 --> 00:06:37.080
across six countries.

00:06:37.080 --> 00:06:42.129
And what comes out of that history is that
for operations to manipulate people, there's

00:06:42.129 --> 00:06:46.610
never a clear answer as to how many people
were manipulated or how many people's minds

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:47.610
were changed.

00:06:47.610 --> 00:06:54.219
It's about making informed analytical judgments
and then orienting future policy based on

00:06:54.219 --> 00:06:56.110
those judgments since the first point.

00:06:56.110 --> 00:06:59.529
The second point is to what Russia did is
Russia did three things.

00:06:59.529 --> 00:07:05.169
The first is Russia systemically manipulated
social media platforms with with propaganda

00:07:05.169 --> 00:07:09.499
in spreading propaganda that advanced its
two objectives to sow discord and division

00:07:09.499 --> 00:07:13.330
and to advantage one candidate over another,
which, by the way, is nothing new.

00:07:13.330 --> 00:07:17.000
I spent about half a day with the former KGB
general and they tried to do both of those

00:07:17.000 --> 00:07:19.800
things in many U.S. elections during the Cold
War.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:22.039
They just didn't have social media to do it.

00:07:22.039 --> 00:07:26.560
The second thing that Russia did was hack
and release sensitive e-mails that were damaging

00:07:26.560 --> 00:07:27.919
to Hillary Clinton's candidacy.

00:07:27.919 --> 00:07:34.370
And the third thing that Russia did was systemically
target our voting systems, which was actually

00:07:34.370 --> 00:07:38.699
what captivated the Obama administration in
the summer and fall because Russian military

00:07:38.699 --> 00:07:44.370
intelligence was scanning, probing and penetrating
our election infrastructure to the point where,

00:07:44.370 --> 00:07:48.720
according to folks like John Brennan, Russia
had the ability to alter the vote tallies

00:07:48.720 --> 00:07:52.869
and voter data of U.S. citizens on Election
Day itself.

00:07:52.869 --> 00:07:59.729
So there's people who will look at that and
they'll say, you know, that's a lot of work

00:07:59.729 --> 00:08:03.479
for ultimately getting Donald Trump elected.

00:08:03.479 --> 00:08:09.430
To the extent that it helped and in the end,
Donald Trump really hasn't done that much.

00:08:09.430 --> 00:08:10.899
That seems great for Russia.

00:08:10.899 --> 00:08:12.909
And you'll have people provide lists on both
sides.

00:08:12.909 --> 00:08:15.460
Here's things that Trump did that seem good
for Russia.

00:08:15.460 --> 00:08:18.319
Here's things Trump did that seemed not so
good for me.

00:08:18.319 --> 00:08:19.960
It's never really been about that.

00:08:19.960 --> 00:08:25.319
It's been about, listen, the U.S. now is a
laughing stock in a way that it was not prior

00:08:25.319 --> 00:08:26.319
to 2016.

00:08:26.319 --> 00:08:31.270
The U.S. is not in conversations about climate
change because Trump says it's a hoax created

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.270
by the Chinese.

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:35.300
The U.S. is increasingly I mean, on coronavirus,
we're not leading.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:39.890
For me, it's not about getting specific concessions.

00:08:39.890 --> 00:08:46.380
It's about questioning how stable is the U.S.
and how clearly are people thinking.

00:08:46.380 --> 00:08:53.090
And it's a bigger picture thing where it's
sort of the downfall of American democracy

00:08:53.090 --> 00:08:57.400
broadly more than about Trump doing things
for Putin.

00:08:57.400 --> 00:09:01.030
Is that the right lens or is it a different
lens we should be thinking of?

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.221
No, you're spot on.

00:09:02.221 --> 00:09:07.200
I think a real misconception is that Putin
Godhra helped to get Trump elected.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:12.110
So therefore, Trump is going to cede Ukraine
to Russia or something like that.

00:09:12.110 --> 00:09:15.760
And that kind of transactional view of why
Trump is of value to Putin.

00:09:15.760 --> 00:09:20.570
And that really misunderstands Putin's foreign
policy and his and his and is his strategy

00:09:20.570 --> 00:09:26.720
really, which is in America, to degrade, disrupt
and discredit American democracy, to corrupt

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:29.520
American this democracy in itself.

00:09:29.520 --> 00:09:35.520
So when Trump causes chaos, when Trump sows
discord, when Trump erodes democratic norms,

00:09:35.520 --> 00:09:41.560
that is the dream of Russia that matters so
much more than what might be happening regarding

00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:43.220
a specific foreign policy decision.

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:48.830
Because what Vladimir Putin wants is for American
democracy to erode, for him to therefore be

00:09:48.830 --> 00:09:52.770
able to say to his own people, see, democracy
doesn't work.

00:09:52.770 --> 00:09:57.340
The story of American democracy was a myth,
and you shouldn't want that.

00:09:57.340 --> 00:10:01.931
It opens up new opportunities for influence
for him, because as America retreats as a

00:10:01.931 --> 00:10:10.360
leader abroad, that means that states will
therefore be more susceptible to Russian influence.

00:10:10.360 --> 00:10:14.780
And it also makes it so that America is so
divided at home, is so disrupted at home that

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:18.780
America can't push back against Russia abroad
and can't engage with Russia in it in a meaningful

00:10:18.780 --> 00:10:19.780
way abroad.

00:10:19.780 --> 00:10:21.940
So Trump could do nothing.

00:10:21.940 --> 00:10:25.570
Transactionally that helped Russia edit the
Trump presidency can be of enormous value

00:10:25.570 --> 00:10:26.770
to Putin.

00:10:26.770 --> 00:10:30.600
And that is the best way to understand what
Trump's presidency has thus far been, for

00:10:30.600 --> 00:10:31.600
example.

00:10:31.600 --> 00:10:36.700
What we see happening in Portland right now,
you know, it's having soldiers or DHS officials

00:10:36.700 --> 00:10:39.060
who don't have marks on their uniforms.

00:10:39.060 --> 00:10:42.570
It's reminiscent of what Putin did in Ukraine
with his soldiers being unmarked.

00:10:42.570 --> 00:10:46.520
And it also shows that America and Russia,
you know, it enables is what about a sort

00:10:46.520 --> 00:10:51.380
of argument that that America should be seeking
to rebut because there is no equivalency or

00:10:51.380 --> 00:10:55.830
should not be between Russian and American
behavior domestically when it comes to the

00:10:55.830 --> 00:10:58.960
other superpower of China.

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:04.780
One of the allegations that has been made
is that Donald Trump specifically asked the

00:11:04.780 --> 00:11:10.120
Chinese president for help when it comes to
farmers, the idea being China buy stuff from

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:11.260
American farmers.

00:11:11.260 --> 00:11:14.890
This helped frumps, helps Trump with the farmers
that helped him get reelected in 2020.

00:11:14.890 --> 00:11:15.890
That's a.

00:11:15.890 --> 00:11:19.560
A really specific ask more broadly, there's
this interview from last year where Trump

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:23.820
was interviewed by George Stephanopoulos and
Stephanopoulos said, if Russia or China came

00:11:23.820 --> 00:11:26.640
to you with information that was useful to
you.

00:11:26.640 --> 00:11:27.640
Would you call the FBI?

00:11:27.640 --> 00:11:28.640
Would you accept it?

00:11:28.640 --> 00:11:31.280
And Trump said, well, yeah, I would look at
it first and then, you know, maybe I'd tell

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:36.230
the FBI, maybe I wouldn't talk a little bit
about either abstractly or concretely the

00:11:36.230 --> 00:11:40.100
role of China in the 2020 election.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:44.500
So I think that's a really open and interesting
question, because 2016 was a turning point

00:11:44.500 --> 00:11:48.670
in this history and a couple of ways, one
of which was it was the first time the issue

00:11:48.670 --> 00:11:52.250
of covered electoral interference was really
broadcast to the world.

00:11:52.250 --> 00:11:57.130
It exited the shadows and it showed China,
Iran, North Korea, whomever.

00:11:57.130 --> 00:12:02.680
You can really disrupt American democracy
with not that much money and with relatively

00:12:02.680 --> 00:12:06.060
simple ideas because of how exposed our country
is.

00:12:06.060 --> 00:12:10.760
So I think the question on my mind is whether
China seeks to imitate and further the Russian

00:12:10.760 --> 00:12:13.920
model or whether this will continue to be
a Russian tradition.

00:12:13.920 --> 00:12:15.450
I don't know the answer to that.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:17.880
I think we will know the answer in the coming
months.

00:12:17.880 --> 00:12:21.630
But I think something that we should be clear
eyed about is that to this point, this has

00:12:21.630 --> 00:12:24.930
been much more a Russian story than a Chinese
story.

00:12:24.930 --> 00:12:30.320
So folks who say China will break new ground
here or North Korea or Iran, and it's as if

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:33.500
everyone's operating from the same starting
point, that's just not true.

00:12:33.500 --> 00:12:36.730
You know, Vladimir Putin worked for the KGB
for 15 years.

00:12:36.730 --> 00:12:40.470
He was a part of an agency that was interfering
in elections all over the world.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:41.820
There's a history here.

00:12:41.820 --> 00:12:44.630
There's a reason why Russia is at the forefront
here.

00:12:44.630 --> 00:12:45.930
And I think we should keep that in mind.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:48.320
And a brief point on Trump.

00:12:48.320 --> 00:12:52.850
I also think Americans really need to keep
in mind that regardless of what he says, this

00:12:52.850 --> 00:12:55.600
is not a political issue.

00:12:55.600 --> 00:12:59.410
If you believe in this thread, that doesn't
make you, you know, a Democrat.

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:02.370
The Soviets targeted Ronald Reagan during
the Cold War.

00:13:02.370 --> 00:13:06.780
A Republican, they targeted Richard Nixon,
a Republican, to destroy their campaigns.

00:13:06.780 --> 00:13:09.900
Now, they just so happened to be helping a
Republican.

00:13:09.900 --> 00:13:11.610
But the point isn't to help a Republican.

00:13:11.610 --> 00:13:15.941
The point is to further the interests of the
Russian state, which is to degrade, corrupt

00:13:15.941 --> 00:13:18.400
and tear down American democracy.

00:13:18.400 --> 00:13:23.090
And that is not in alignment with the interests
of any American citizen, regardless of political

00:13:23.090 --> 00:13:24.090
party.

00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:30.130
So to touch on 2020 and Russia, then if you
look at the polls now, they certainly don't

00:13:30.130 --> 00:13:32.530
look good for Donald Trump.

00:13:32.530 --> 00:13:35.570
But as I've been telling my audience, you
have to assume nothing.

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:38.850
You have to vote as if your vote is the deciding
vote in your state.

00:13:38.850 --> 00:13:42.020
That's really the only the only intelligent
way forward.

00:13:42.020 --> 00:13:48.520
But this does Russia's ability to medal become
diminished if indeed the election is not close?

00:13:48.520 --> 00:13:51.440
Or do their priorities change or how does
that affect things?

00:13:51.440 --> 00:13:56.020
So their priorities change because another
myth here is that Russian interference is

00:13:56.020 --> 00:13:58.690
just about getting Donald Trump elected again.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:13:59.690
Not true.

00:13:59.690 --> 00:14:04.440
Russia's operation to interfere in the 2016
elections started in 2014 before Trump even

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:06.060
announced his candidacy.

00:14:06.060 --> 00:14:10.250
And as I reveal in my book, based on my interviews
with John Brennan and Jim Clapper, Russia

00:14:10.250 --> 00:14:16.290
had plans to continue interfering in our politics
to undermine Hillary Clinton had she won the

00:14:16.290 --> 00:14:17.290
election.

00:14:17.290 --> 00:14:21.470
And they were basically starting that operation
before Trump even won, which surprised Putin.

00:14:21.470 --> 00:14:27.320
So as we await Election Day now, it's important
to keep in mind that the foremost Russian

00:14:27.320 --> 00:14:31.860
objective, again, is to undermine our democracy,
to sow doubt about the functioning of our

00:14:31.860 --> 00:14:32.860
democracy.

00:14:32.860 --> 00:14:37.920
And, yes, Trump might be losing, but new opportunities
emerge, such as if Donald Trump is alleging

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.640
that the election will be rigged.

00:14:39.640 --> 00:14:43.750
It is in Russia's interests for Americans
to believe their election is rigged.

